# JNLisp CFD FVM Package

- Author: Jed Nelson
- Date: 27/11/25

High level FVM interactions for CFD workflows.


## Fields

Creates context from mesh and initializes empty field storage.
j(defn make-context [mesh]
  (.make-context mesh))

Adds a field with per-cell values to context.
j(defn add-field! [ctx name vals]
  (.add-field ctx name vals))

Adds a field with uniform value across all cells to context.
j(defn add-uniform-field! [ctx name val]
  (.add-uniform-field ctx name val))

Adds a field with single constant value to context.
j(defn add-constant-field! [ctx name val]
  (.add-constant-field ctx name val))

Sets field values for cells in named region.
j(defn set-region-vals! [ctx fname regname val]
  (.set-region-vals ctx fname regname val))


## Expressions

Expression constructors enable field arithmetic without runtime overhead.

Creates expression from field name in context.
j(defn expr-field [ctx name]
  (.expr-field ctx name))

Creates constant expression with fixed value.
j(defn expr-const [val]
  (.expr-const val))

Multiplies two expressions.
j(defn expr-mul [e1 e2]
  (.expr-mul e1 e2))

Adds two expressions.
j(defn expr-add [e1 e2]
  (.expr-add e1 e2))

Subtracts two expressions.
j(defn expr-sub [e1 e2]
  (.expr-sub e1 e2))

Divides two expressions.
j(defn expr-quot [e1 e2]
  (.expr-quot e1 e2))


## Equations

Creates equation on mesh for named field.
j(defn make-equation [mesh]
  (.make-equation mesh))

Zeros equation coefficients for reuse.
j(defn zero! [eq]
  (.equation-zero eq))

Solves equation with given solver and writes solution to named field.
j(defn solve! [eq solver ctx fname]
  (.equation-solve eq solver ctx fname))


## Operators

Operators accumulate coefficients into equation matrices. They mutate the equation in place and return it for threading.

Adds Laplacian term to equation with gamma diffusivity.
j(defn laplacian! [eq ctx phi gamma]
  (.laplacian eq ctx phi gamma))

Adds linearized source term to equation.
j(defn source! [eq ctx phi su sp]
  (.source eq ctx phi su sp))


## Boundary Conditions

Boundary conditions modify equation coefficients and source terms. They are applied after flux operators accumulate boundary fluxes.

Applies Dirichlet boundary condition with fixed value.
j(defn bc-dirichlet! [eq ctx bname val]
  (.bc-dirichlet eq ctx bname val))

Applies Neumann boundary condition with fixed flux.
j(defn bc-neumann! [eq ctx bname val]
  (.bc-neumann eq ctx bname val))

Applies Robin boundary condition with mixed coefficients.
j(defn bc-robin! [eq ctx bname alpha gamma]
  (.bc-robin eq ctx bname alpha gamma))


## High-level helpers

Threading helper for equation assembly.
j(defn assemble [eq ...ops]
  (reduce (fn [e op] (op e)) eq ops))
